    "text": "Let C1 , . . . , Cn be (left or right) cosets of a finite group G such that U :=\nC1 ∪ · · · ∪ Cn is not G. Is it always true that |G \\ U | ⩾ |G|/2n ?\n   Affirmative answers are known in some special cases (B. Sambale, M. Tărnăuceanu,\nJ. Algebraic Combin., 55 (2022), 979–987).                                    B. Sambale",
